        <dc:title>Jack Reacher's Rules</dc:title>
        <dc:creator opf:file-as="Child, Lee" opf:role="aut">Lee Child</dc:creator>
        <dc:contributor opf:file-as="calibre" opf:role="bkp">calibre (1.48.0) [http://calibre-ebook.com]</dc:contributor>
        <dc:date>2012-11-06T00:00:00+00:00</dc:date>
        <dc:description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;"I'm not afraid of death, death's afraid of me."--Jack Reacher&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;  &lt;br&gt; You don't have to break the rules if you &lt;i&gt;make&lt;/i&gt; the rules. Case in point: Jack Reacher, the two-fisted, quick-witted, "current poster-boy of American crime fiction" (&lt;i&gt;Los Angeles Times&lt;/i&gt;). The brainchild of #1 &lt;i&gt;New York Times&lt;/i&gt; bestselling author Lee Child, Reacher is a freelance troubleshooter with a mysterious past--and a serious passion for justice. Now all his hard-won knowledge and hard-hitting strategies are within every thriller reader's reach--in a rapid-fire rundown of all the trade secrets, tried-and-true tricks, and time-honored tactics that separate the man in the street from the man to beat:&lt;br&gt;  &lt;br&gt; &lt;b&gt;&amp;bull; Never count on anything except surprise and unpredictability and danger.&lt;li&gt;Go to bed fully clothed so you are always ready for action.&lt;li&gt;Next to a shotgun, a pool cue is the best weapon in a fight.&lt;li&gt;Look, don't see, listen, don't hear. The more you engage, the...</dc:description>
